# Bytes as a signed 16-bit integer `i16`: a 2-byte chain reinterpreted
# as two's complement. For any other length the `cant-convert` fallback
# takes an error message. When unbound, it terminates with that message.

+architect yegor256@gmail.com
+home https://github.com/objectionary/eo
+package bytes
+spdx SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2016-2026 Objectionary.com
+spdx SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+unlint invalid-name-notation
+version 0.0.0

[^data cant-convert] > as-i16
  if. > @
    data.size.eq 2
    i16 data
    cant-convert
      "Can't convert non 2 length bytes to i16, bytes are %x".printf
        * data

  00-33.as-i16.as-bytes.eq 00-33 ++> can-convert-bytes-to-i16-and-back

  eq. ++> can-recover-from-bytes-of-wrong-size-when-converting-to-i16
    i16 7F-3C
    C8-.as-i16
      i16 7F-3C > [message]

  01-01-01.as-i16 --> stops-on-bytes-of-wrong-size-when-converting-to-i16
